{
  "name": "Draft replies to social media comments with AI and approve them in Slack with Rizamo",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Draft replies to comments with AI and approve them in Slack\n\n### How it works\nFor brands and agencies that answer every comment but want a person to check each reply. When a comment arrives on an Instagram, Facebook, TikTok, YouTube or Threads post, OpenAI drafts a short reply in the comment's language. Spam and comments that need a person, such as complaints, are skipped.\n\nSlack then shows the comment and the draft with **Reply** and **Skip** buttons, and the workflow waits. Rizamo posts the reply under the comment only when someone chooses Reply. A draft cannot be edited from Slack: skip it and answer in Rizamo's inbox instead.\n\n### Setup\n1. Install the verified community node `@rizamohq/n8n-nodes-rizamo` (tested with 0.1.1): open the nodes panel, search **Rizamo** and choose **Install** ([installation guide](https://docs.n8n.io/integrations/community-nodes/installation/verified-install/)).\n2. In Rizamo, open **Developers**, create an API key and add it in n8n as a **Rizamo API** credential.\n3. Connect OpenAI in **Draft a reply** and edit its instructions to your brand's voice.\n4. Connect Slack and pick the channel in **Ask for approval**.\n5. Activate the workflow. **New comment** creates its webhook in Rizamo, which needs an https address: n8n Cloud has one, and a self-hosted n8n needs a public one.\n\n### Customization\nPick profiles in **New comment** to answer one brand only, or change the model and its instructions in **Draft a reply**.",
        "height": 820,
        "width": 520
      },
      "id": "ff29ed45-bd06-5c06-a01b-a9de6c746960",
      "name": "About",
